wn but not counted; snigdha and 潤 = Moist, rūkṣa and 燥 = Dry.", "sources": [{"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool); agrees with the app moisture (dry).", "assigns_moisture": "Dry", "assigns_temperature": "Cool", "corpus": "galenic-european", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": true, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "Meadow-Sweet is cold and dry, with an evident binding quality adjoined.", "gloss": "Meadowsweet is cold and dry.", "locator": "Book II, Chap. 419 'Of Meadow-Sweet, or Queen of the Meadows', The Temperature", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Gerard (1633)", "source": "John Gerard, The Herball or Generall Historie of Plantes, enlarged by Thomas Johnson (1633 text; read in the Ex-Classics transcription and checked against the 1636 printing scanned at archive.org)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://www.exclassics.com/herbal/herball.txt", "year": "1633"}, {"agreement": "Counted: differs from the app temperature (source neutral, app cool); agrees with the app moisture (dry).", "assigns_moisture": "Dry", "assigns_temperature": "Neutral", "corpus": "galenic-european", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": true, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "VII. The Qualities. Mede-Sweet is temperate in refpe&t to heat or cold, bur dry in the firft Degree. Abfterfive, Aftringent, and Traumatick, or Vulnerary", "gloss": "Meadowsweet is temperate as to heat or cold, but dry in the first degree.", "locator": "Chapter 'Of MEDE-SWEET' (Ulmaria, Regina prati), The Qualities (OCR at offset 3818170; the chapter number on the page is not legible)", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "", "short": "Salmon (1710)", "source": "William Salmon, Botanologia: The English Herbal (London, 1710)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://archive.org/download/gri_33125012917387/gri_33125012917387_djvu.txt", "year": "1710"}], "sources_agree": false, "stored_before": {"moisture": "